# Build context for `docker build -f backtester/Dockerfile .` (the local path
# documented in backtester/README.md).
#
# This file lives at the REPO ROOT because that is the only place Docker reads
# it from. It used to live at backtester/.dockerignore, where Docker never read
# it — the proof is that it shipped as a regular file inside the published
# image, at /app/backtester/.dockerignore. Its patterns were already written
# relative to the repo root (`backtester/tests`, `data/cache`), i.e. authored
# for this location; only the filename's directory was wrong. BuildKit does
# honour a sibling `<dockerfile>.dockerignore`, but that name would have to be
# `backtester/Dockerfile.dockerignore`, and Cloud Build's docker builder is the
# classic one, which has no such lookup at all.
#
# Deploys go through `gcloud builds submit`, which filters the upload with
# /.gcloudignore first; the two files must stay compatible. Neither may ever
# exclude something the Dockerfile COPYs — in particular data/market/ohlcv,
# which is gitignored in some checkouts but MUST reach the build.

.git
.gitignore
.worktrees
.venv
venv
.claude
.superpowers

# The Astro site is deployed separately by Vercel; the service never reads it.
site

# Notebooks, plans, specs and generated reports — none are build inputs.
docs
notebooks

# The service has no test runner in the image.
**/tests
**/conftest.py

# Local caches and test artefacts.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.hypothesis
htmlcov
.coverage
.DS_Store
**/.env*

# Data trees the Dockerfile does not COPY, listed so a future `COPY data`
# typo cannot silently pull them in.
data/cache
data/agent_memory
data/output
data/blog
data/posts
